    "body": "<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\n## Working session summary\n\nThe fix, tests, docs, and changelog are committed and pushed to `issue-190-247187104443`; PR #200 is updated. CI run 31969120220 is still in progress — I'll report as soon as it finishes.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `src/token.rs` — `issue_with_id` returns the JWT together with its store record id (`sub`); `issue` delegates to it.\n- `src/clients/credentials.rs` (new) — secret-free `ManagedCredential` record (`source`, `token_id`, `label`, `issued_at`), written 0600 next to the env file. This was the missing metadata: without it, remove had no way to name the token it was deleting.\n- `src/client_command.rs` — setup persists the record after writing the secret; `remove` revokes **before** deleting, and on revocation failure keeps both files, prints `tokens revoke <ID>` recovery instructions, and exits 1 instead of reporting success.\n- `src/cli.rs` — `clients remove --revoke-supplied` (operator-supplied tokens are otherwise left alone) and `--force` (escape hatch).\n- `tests/clients_token_revocation_test.rs` — 5 black-box tests across 6 client integrations × both persistent backends, including a live `serve` process that answers 401/403 with the removed credential, and a fresh-process `tokens list` that doubles as the restart-persistence check.\n- Docs (`configure-clients.md`, `cli-agent.md`) and a `bump: minor` changelog fragment.\n\n`with`/`with --global` needed no change — per-run credentials already go through `cleanup_run_credential`, and `--global` persists no credential of its own. Locally `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features` (clean), the file-size limit, and the full `cargo test` suite all pass.\n\nPR: https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/200 — I have not run `gh pr ready 200` yet, since CI hasn't reported.\n\n---\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*",
